+# Best AI Tools for Insurance Agents in 2026
+
+[![Awesome](https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/sindresorhus/awesome@main/media/badge.svg)](https://github.com/sindresorhus/awesome)
+[![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-yellow.svg)](https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT)
+![Topics](https://img.shields.io/github/stars/GagnDeep/awesome-best-ai-tools-for-insurance-agents-2026?style=social)
+
+> The best AI tools for insurance agents in 2026 are not niche insurance-branded SaaS apps. They are open-source GitHub projects for document intake, OCR, PDF parsing, retrieval, voice transcription, and workflow automation that insurance agencies can self-host and adapt for quoting, underwriting support, claims intake, policy search, call notes, and compliance-heavy back-office work. This list only includes public GitHub repositories and avoids closed proprietary SaaS products.
+
+## Table of Contents
+- [TL;DR](#tldr)
+- [Why This List](#why-this-list)
+- [Open Source Tools](#open-source-tools)
+- [FAQ](#faq)
+- [Contributing](#contributing)
