+- **Best for:** Normalizing mixed-format insurance documents into a standard schema
+
+---
+
+#### [OpenOCR](https://github.com/Topdu/OpenOCR)
+> **Description:** OpenOCR is positioned as a general OCR research and application toolkit that combines benchmarks, document parsing systems, and implementations from academic papers. For insurance teams, the appeal is breadth: text detection, recognition, table understanding, and document parsing are all relevant to intake automation, especially for multilingual agencies or global brokers. It is Apache-2.0 licensed and relatively new compared with older OCR stacks, but the repository is active and clearly aimed at practical OCR workflows rather than only model demos. That makes it a credible option for teams testing alternatives to the dominant OCR toolchains.
+
+- **GitHub:** [github.com/Topdu/OpenOCR](https://github.com/Topdu/OpenOCR)
