+#### [OCRmyPDF](https://github.com/ocrmypdf/OCRmyPDF)
+> **Description:** OCRmyPDF is a pragmatic command-line tool for adding an OCR text layer to scanned PDFs while preserving the original pages and producing searchable PDF/A output. In insurance, that is extremely practical: many agencies simply need to make incoming scans searchable before archiving or indexing them. The README calls out rotation fixes, deskewing, metadata handling, multiple languages through Tesseract, and scriptable automation. It is MPL-2.0 licensed and well maintained. If your main problem is not “build an AI agent” but “make carrier packets and old files searchable,” OCRmyPDF is one of the best open-source choices.
