+#### [pdfplumber](https://github.com/jsvine/pdfplumber)
+> **Description:** pdfplumber is a detailed PDF extraction library that focuses on characters, lines, rectangles, tables, and visual debugging for machine-generated PDFs. For insurance agencies, this is useful when documents are already digital and the main need is extracting text, fields, or tables from policy schedules, statements, or reports without OCR. The README is explicit that it works best on machine-generated PDFs, which is the right expectation to set. It is MIT licensed and mature. pdfplumber is a strong fit for back-office tooling that needs accurate PDF parsing rather than a full end-user AI interface.
